# Generated compiler and site output belongs to no language statistic and is
# hidden from diffs.
dist/** linguist-generated
examples/*/dist/** linguist-generated

# github-linguist has no Eliscript entry. The previous line here used
# `linguist-language=Lisp`, which Linguist resolves through its alias table to
# Common Lisp, so the repository reported a language it does not contain. A
# name Linguist does not know cannot be used instead: the attribute is ignored
# and the file falls back to the extension map, which has no entry for `.eli`.
#
# The sources are therefore excluded from the language bar rather than
# attributed to a language they are not. GitHub can only report, colour, and
# highlight "Eliscript" once an entry exists upstream: `lib/linguist/languages.yml`
# needs `type`, `color`, `extensions: [".eli"]`, `tm_scope`, and `aliases`,
# together with a syntax grammar added by `script/add-grammar`, samples under
# `samples/`, and an id from `script/update-ids`.
*.eli linguist-detectable=false
